 AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:33372656") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4023121 "long-range GABAergic interneuron")
-AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:15845086") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:26727548") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:27618674") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30382198") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:33186530") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:34302742") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:40403704") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:40997796") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:42717094") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023121 "Not classified as either local interneuron (CL:0004001) or projection neuron (CL:9900000), because the evidence differs between the cortical and striatal members of this class. Cerebral cortex: these cells are projection neurons. Long-range cortical GABAergic neurons identified by retrograde labelling are mostly somatostatin-, NPY- and nNOS-positive and lie in layer II, layer VI and white matter (PMID:15845086). The transcriptomic Sst-Chodl type was matched to these Nos1-positive long-range projecting cells by marker expression, location and Cre-line labelling, not by retrograde labelling of transcriptomically typed cells (PMID:26727548, PMID:27618674, PMID:30382198); Patch-seq maps the deep-layer, non-Martinotti, long-range projecting Sst-MET-1 type to Sst Chodl (PMID:33186530). Direct evidence comes from single-cell reconstructions of Sst;Chodl intersectionally labelled mouse cells, which have dense local arbors plus intracortical, mainly ipsilateral axons extending millimetres across most neocortical areas (PMID:42717094); see also PMID:40997796. Striatum: Sst-Chodl cells correspond to the Sst/Npy/Nos1 low-threshold spiking interneurons, which are described as local interneurons whose processes stay within the striatum (PMID:34302742, PMID:40403704); no striatal Sst-Chodl projection outside the striatum has been reported. Region-specific subclasses can be classified as projection neuron (cortex) or local interneuron (striatum). The label keeps 'interneuron' to match existing usage and the WMB taxonomy (CCN20230722).")
